{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-23T14:31:15.023Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ae79e01579ce628b9886631b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-23T14:31:15.023Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-23T14:31:15.022Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Overlap recheck: current host is 2026.10.23; pinned SDK is 2026.10.15 and remains unchanged. Core workspace snapshots/history replay, extension capabilities and MCP authorization do not define native selective object archives. Sibling pm-context serves projected context with omission receipts; pm-swarm lanes and pm-web access controls do not bind native closure and replay authorization in a signed manifest. Reuse native bundle hashing/closure, object-store lease, ref CAS, signature key parsing, SDK extension registration/rendering/testing and PmClient tracker operations. Existing forge transport and tenant authorization remain primitives; Phase 6 streaming and pm-vcs-uploadretention receipt expiry remain separate backlog. Contract: select exact native tips and explicit permitted paths/ref names; carry their full ancestry without rewriting identities; refuse histories that reference paths outside scope. Inventory excluded physical objects without payload disclosure; partial or erased source state prevents a source completeness claim. Receiver independently supplies scope, trusted keys and expected ref values before import."}]}],"before_hash":"ee9e06a41cdb34e35da30e36c4b43a2e7810e58baef955b9f515f941085cac69","after_hash":"e7829a4cc2700209f57dad0a5fe62cac14cccab15a295d4b02c2e54bc77479cf","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved",